# Best Coding Practices (Frontend)

- Write clear, maintainable, and testable code with small focused units.
- Prefer readability over clever shortcuts.
- Keep components and functions single-purpose.
- Use consistent naming for files, components, hooks, and variables.
- Avoid duplicated logic; extract shared utilities/components where useful.
- Handle errors explicitly and provide user-safe fallbacks.
- Keep side effects controlled and predictable.
- Remove dead code and avoid unused imports/variables.
- Add brief comments only when business logic is not obvious.
- Keep changes scoped to the requested feature; avoid unrelated refactors.

- Follow project conventions:
  - Reuse shared UI from `commonUI`.
  - Use theme tokens instead of repeated hardcoded styles.
  - Use i18next keys for user-facing text.
